  "title": "Back to School: A Visit to Mwalimu Akinyi",
  "category": "people",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "level": 4,
  "order": 403,
  "theme": "school",
  "culturalNote": "Kenyan schools run from 8 a.m., in uniforms (sare) of bright colours, and every child knows the head teacher as \"mwalimu mkuu\". Pupils sit national exams at the end of primary and secondary school, and parents talk about results constantly. Classes are counted, not named: darasa la nne is \"class four\". Teachers are addressed simply as \"mwalimu\" (teacher) — it's a title of respect.",
  "startingPoint": "Your friend Akinyi is the head teacher of a primary school in Kibera. She's invited you to visit.",
